cludes her report.  ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: \n<span class=\"bullet\">Proofread the sentence. </span> \n<span class=\"bullet\">Click on the incorrect words. </span> \n<span class=\"bullet\">Type in the correct words to complete the sentence. </span>  <span class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary.</span> ", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": 2, "type": "template_override"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}]}], "id": 10, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 0, "selected": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn6le02ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le02ob11re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn6le02ob11re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn6le02ob11re2img01.jpg", "text": "Aung San Suu Kyi has helped fight for her country's struggle for democracy since 1988. She was born to lead her nation; her father was Myanmar's independence hero. He was tragically assassinated when she was just two years old. Suu Kyi had an international upbringing. She has studied in Myanmar, India, and the United Kingdom.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn6le02ob11re2img02.jpg", "text": "In 1988, she returned home to care for her ill mother. Myanmar was in political chaos after a new military group took power. A nationwide uprising started and Suu Kyi tirelessly campaigned for freedom and democracy. She was determined to help her people and fight the dictators who led her country.", "time": "24000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn6le02ob11re2img03.jpg", "text": "She was arrested and offered her freedom back if she left the country, but she blatantly refused. She has won the Nobel Peace Prize. She was released from prison on November 13th, 2010. She was kindly greeted by thousands of adoring Burmese at the gates of her home.", "time": "46500", "id": 3}]}}], "id": 1}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Famous People", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Fighting for Freedom", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le02ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past vs. Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "She became a national figure. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She has studied in many countries around the world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Action is over and has no connection to present \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use \u201ced\u201d for regular verbs.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Action happened in the past, but there is some connection to the present, action may still be happening in the present \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"use \u201chave or has\u201d and past participle of verb.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbs of Manner", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use adverbs of manner to describe how something is done.</p>  Example: She blatantly refused their offers.</br> How did she refuse their offers? Blatantly.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "She immediately took an interest in the politics of the country.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She actively campaigned against the military groups.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Many adverbs are formed by adding -ly to an adjective: </br>Examples:    \tkind \u2192 kindly &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;          \ttireless \u2192 tirelessly </p>  Some adverbs are formed by adding -ally.</br> Example:  tragic \u2192  tragically </p>  These adverbs can come after the direct object or after the verb if there isn't any direct object.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fight for", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the process of trying to achieve something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She has helped her country fight for freedom.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le02ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are the words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "upbringing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way that your parents care for you and teach you to behave when you are growing up", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She had an international upbringing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le02ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to assassinate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to kill an important person", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Her father was assassinated when she was two years old. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le02ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Myanmar ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a country in southeast Asia, to the east of India which was called Burma until 1998", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: India is between Myanmar and Pakistan.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le02ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to campaign", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take part in a series of actions intended to achieve a specific result", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She campaigned against the military group. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le02ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "determined", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a strong desire to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She was determined to help her people.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le02ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Review all the lessons. Write down the names of all the women you learned about. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose one of them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down 8-10 questions you would ask them. Remember to ask about their experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your questions. Practice reading them aloud.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write down interview questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about people's past experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice reading my interview questions aloud.", "type": "text"}]}]}